{
  "_meta": {
    "step": "birthright",
    "source": "Rogue Trader Core Rulebook + Into the Storm",
    "status": "Core reconciled-by-hand from Core book pp.24-25. Into the Storm 'New Birthright Options' reconciled from ItS pp.17-20 (printed folios; PDF pages 18-21). Verify vs errata.",
    "scope": "Core (Scavenger/Scapegrace/Stubjack/Child of the Creed/Savant/Vaunted) plus the nine Into the Storm advanced Birthright picks. ItS groups three sub-options under each broad heading (Fringe Survivor / Unnatural Origin / In Service to the Throne); each concrete sub-option is its own selectable record carrying its printed xp_cost (ItS p.17: 'pick a single option ... and pay the listed amount of xp'), named 'Heading - Option' (matching INC 1's Lure convention). The broad heading 'may be taken instead of' two Core birthrights (recorded as substitutes_for). XP costs verified against ItS page text AND the AllowStorm-gated Excel StormBirthrightOptionList (all nine match). ItS Advanced Origins is the human path, so each ItS pick requires species Human.",
    "rules_qa": [
      "Provenance pages are PRINTED FOLIOS (ItS folio = PDF page index - 1).",
      "Fringe Survivor (instead of Scavenger or Savant) -> Survivalist 300 (+3 T or Per; Survival trained; +1 Fate; 1d5+1 Insanity), Heretek 100 (+3 Int; choose TWO from Chem-Use/Common Lore (Tech)/Forbidden Lore (Archeotech)/Tech-Use/Medicae/Scholastic Lore (any) trained; 1d5+1 Corruption), Pit-Fighter 200 (+3 T or S and +3 WS; Rival (Underworld); 1 Corruption).",
      "Unnatural Origin (instead of Scapegrace or Stubjack) -> Contaminated Environs 100 (Peer (Mutants)+Resistance (Poisons); +3 T or WP; -3 Fel; optional +100xp roll on Mutation table re-rolling 75+), False-Man 300 (Ambidextrous+Autosanguine+Chem-Geld; +3 to two chosen characteristics; -3 to one chosen; either 2d10 Insanity OR lose 1 Fate permanently), Tainted by the Warp 200 (Dark Soul+Jaded; Forbidden Lore (Warp) as untrained basic; +3 Per or WP; -3 Fel; 1d10 Corruption; optional +300xp Favoured by the Warp + another 1d10 Corruption).",
      "In Service to the Throne (instead of Child of the Creed or Vaunted) -> Tithed 350 (one Common Lore trained from a 7-item list; choose TWO skills/talents from a long list; see note), Born to Lead 200 (Command+Literacy+one Scholastic Lore from {Bureaucracy, Imperial Creed, Judgement, Tactica Imperialis} trained; +3 Int or Fel; -3 T), One Amongst Billions 200 (Paranoia+Unremarkable; one Trade or Common Lore trained; +3 Per or Int; -3 S).",
      "Tithed's 'choose two' second list is long and mixes skills (Drive (any one), Literacy, Medicae, Navigation (surface), Survival, Tech-Use) and weapon-training talents (Basic Weapon Training (Las/SP), Pistol Weapon Training (Las/SP)); the 'choose two' is modelled as two nested choices each offering the full list. Plus +3 Willpower OR Ballistic Skill.",
      "'Choose N from a list' has no native effect type; modelled as N independent nested 'choice' effects each offering the full list (a player could in principle pick the same entry twice -- flag for QA if strict distinctness is required).",
      "Contaminated Environs (mutation roll, +100xp) and Tainted by the Warp (Favoured by the Warp, +300xp) optional extra-xp purchases are modelled as nested 'choice' effects whose 'take it' option carries an origin_xp_cost (hard-debited from the 500 pool, blocking on overspend) plus the granted effect; the 'skip' option (the default) costs nothing."
    ],
